section.para:
&sleminvm; comes with the &combustion; configuration tool, which configures the system on
first boot from a script that you supply. This can be particularly useful when you need to
deploy multiple virtual machines with an identical initial configuration. When &combustion;
runs successfully, &jeosfirstboot; does not start. Because &minimalvm; does not configure a
default &rootuser; password, the script must include a login method, either a &rootuser;
password or an SSH public key for remote access.
